{"amendments":[{"body":"`crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs:153-166` still documents `probe_biofilter_scaling_bigger_media_faster_cycling` as proving that 2× media yields a larger nitrifier population/faster cycling, but `:246-263` now only checks that both runs clear a fixed `0.02 g` floor. On the current branch the large-filter run finishes with less nitrifier biomass than the small filter and still passes, so this probe no longer guards the behavior it is named and documented to validate.","rationale":"The change weakens the test enough that it passes even when the supposed scaling effect is absent."},{"body":"`crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs:627-631` says the redox probe should verify that denitrifier activity matures over time, but `:658-659` now seeds `denitrifier_activity_index = 1.0` and `:847-853` only asserts that the final value stays above `0.5`. That no longer exercises the ramp/decay logic in `crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:973-989`; a bug that prevents maturation or breaks the suboxic-zone coupling would still pass.","rationale":"This removes coverage of the dynamic behavior the probe claims to validate."},{"body":"`crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs:660-662` gives the “planted” arm `10.0 g` decomposer biomass while `:740-741` gives the inert control only `2.0 g`, and `:711-713` zeroes all plant biomass. Because substrate O2 demand is driven directly by decomposer biomass in `crates/tank_core/src/systems/substrate.rs:221-236`, the comparison is now confounded: the test can pass from the artificially higher decomposer-driven suboxia even if the planted-substrate mechanism regresses, and it no longer actually exercises a live-planted setup despite the test name/docs.","rationale":"The probe is no longer isolating the effect it claims to measure."}],"summary":"Found three substantive review issues, all in the modified harness probes: the biofilter probe no longer validates its stated scaling behavior, and the redox probe was both weakened (activity no longer has to mature) and confounded by asymmetric decomposer loading / removed plants."}